REM  tilasm.pni — the immersive cycler.  طلسم
REM  A station is a PLACE, not a moment. There is no timeline here and the
REM  visitor is not on rails: the work is a graph they walk.

CYCLER TILASM
  TITLE   "Tilasm"
  SCRIPT  "طلسم"
  OUTPUT  IMMERSIVE
  UNIT    "station"
  PURPOSE "Build somewhere a person can be: an exhibition, a training environment, a spatial narrative, a virtual laboratory."

  CONTRACT
    REFUSE    "a piece in which no station leads anywhere"
    REFUSE    "an exit naming a station that does not exist"
    REFUSE    "assuming a standing visitor with two hands and hearing"
    INVARIANT "every station has a comfort note, even when the answer is that nothing is needed"
    EVIDENCE  "the exit graph, traversable"
    EVIDENCE  "a stated floor-space requirement and locomotion mode"
  END CONTRACT

  REM ── Start here. Not with a space — with what a person is going to DO in it. ──

  STAGE CONCEPT
    RESOLUTION EASY
    VERB   CREATE
    EXPECT JSON
    INTO   book
    ASK
      I want to build somewhere a person can be. Help me work out what it is.

      Reply with ONLY this JSON:

      {"title":"…","kind":"exhibition|training|narrative|laboratory|interactive place",
       "hardware":"headset, handheld, projected, or a room",
       "visitor":"who arrives, knowing what","doing":"what they DO, as a verb",
       "leaves_with":"what they take away","room":"the floor space this needs",
       "done_when":"…"}

      doing: a verb. "Experiences" and "explores" are not verbs for this purpose — walk,
      assemble, choose, measure, refuse, wait.
      room: a real number in metres, or "seated" — the piece is unbuildable without it.

      What I have so far:
      {seed}
    END ASK
    VALIDATE HAS(book, "doing")
    ON FAIL CLARIFY
  END STAGE

  STAGE REACH
    RESOLUTION MID
    VERB   VERIFY
    EXPECT TEXT
    FROM   book
    INTO   book.reach
    ASK
      Before any station is designed: in 60 to 110 words, who is shut out of this piece as
      conceived, and what would let them in?

      Consider a visitor who cannot stand, who has one hand free, who cannot hear, who gets
      motion sick, and who has two square metres and no more. For each, either say how they
      take part or say plainly that they cannot and why.

      Do not offer a mitigation you have invented. If there is not one, that is the answer.
    END ASK
    VALIDATE NOT EMPTY(book.reach)
    ON FAIL REPAIR
  END STAGE


  STAGE STATIONS
    RESOLUTION EASY
    VERB   CREATE
    EXPECT LIST
    INTO   stations
    ASK
      An immersive piece, "{book}", for {mode}. Break it into stations: places a
      visitor stands, looks and acts.

      Reply with ONLY a JSON array, in the order a visitor meets them:
      [{"anchor":"…","title":"…","beat":"…","exits":["…"]}]

      anchor: where it is — a room, a surface, a marker, "wherever the visitor is".
      exits:  the stations reachable from it. A visitor is not on rails.
    END ASK
    VALIDATE COUNT(stations) > 0
  END STAGE

  STAGE PLACE
    RESOLUTION EASY
    VERB   CREATE
    EXPECT TEXT
    REPEAT FOREACH stations
    INTO   station.lead
    ASK
      Station {station.title}, anchored at {station.anchor}.
      ONE paragraph of 50 to 90 words: what a visitor sees and hears standing there,
      in the vocabulary the piece uses. Do not say it is immersive or breathtaking.
    END ASK
  END STAGE

  STAGE ACT
    RESOLUTION MID
    VERB   CREATE
    EXPECT TEXT
    FROM   station.lead
    INTO   station.interaction
    ASK
      Same station. What can the visitor DO here and what answers them? Name the input
      plainly — gaze, a hand, a controller, a step, a spoken word — and say what happens
      if they do nothing at all, because most visitors will. 50 to 90 words.
    END ASK
  END STAGE

  STAGE COMFORT
    RESOLUTION MID
    VERB   VERIFY
    EXPECT TEXT
    INTO   station.comfort
    ASK
      Same station. In 40 to 80 words state plainly: whether the visitor moves and how;
      anything that could make someone unwell and what mitigates it; what a visitor who
      cannot stand, cannot use both hands, or cannot hear does instead; and the floor
      space this station needs.

      If a hazard has no mitigation, say so rather than inventing one.
    END ASK
    VALIDATE NOT EMPTY(station.comfort)
    ON FAIL REPAIR
  END STAGE

  STAGE ASSET
    RESOLUTION PRO
    VERB   CREATE
    EXPECT MODEL
    OPTIONAL
    ATTACH INBOX
    ASK
      Make the visual for station {station.title}: a glTF/GLB model, or a 360 panorama
      if the station is a place rather than an object. Save it and bring it back.
    END ASK
  END STAGE

  STAGE ABSTRACT
    RESOLUTION MID
    VERB   INTEGRATE
    EXPECT TEXT
    FROM   stations
    INTO   book.description
    ASK
      Deposit abstract for "{book}", an immersive piece in {count} stations.
      Two or three HTML paragraphs in <p> tags.
    END ASK
  END STAGE

  STAGE MINT
    RESOLUTION PRO
    VERB  INTEGRATE
    GATE  HUMAN "MINT tilasm"
    EMIT  DOI
  END STAGE
END CYCLER
